-- ccc27-s743-imprisonment.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 743 to 744 (imprisonment: the default maximum, where it is served,
-- the non-communication order, youth sentences, the power to delay parole eligibility, delivery to the prison).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
-- Answers are `MAYBE BOOLEAN` (or a MAYBE of a type): JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, NOTHING elsewhere.
-- Section 743.4 is shown repealed (nothing to encode). Section 744's duty is also a regulative rule (below).

§ `Section 743 -- Imprisonment when no other provision`

-- src:16049 | 743 Every one who is convicted of an indictable offence for which no punishment is specially provided is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years.
@ref s 743 (src:16049)
GIVEN `the offender is convicted of an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a punishment is specially provided for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Imprisonment
`s 743 the maximum imprisonment for the offence` MEANS
    IF `the offender is convicted of an indictable offence` AND (NOT (`a punishment is specially provided for the offence`))
    THEN JUST (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an indictable offence for which no punishment is specially provided"

-- src:16049 | 743 Every one who is convicted of an indictable offence for which no punishment is specially provided is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years.
@ref s 743 (src:16049)
GIVEN `the offender is convicted of an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a punishment is specially provided for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743 the offender is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years` MEANS
    IF `the offender is convicted of an indictable offence` AND (NOT (`a punishment is specially provided for the offence`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an indictable offence for which no punishment is specially provided"

§ `Section 743.1 -- Where the sentence is served`

-- src:16051 | 743.1 (1) Except where otherwise provided, a person who is sentenced to imprisonment for
-- src:16052 | (a) life,
-- src:16053 | (b) a term of two years or more, or
-- src:16054 | (c) two or more terms of less than two years each that are to be served one after the other and that, in the aggregate, amount to two years or more,
-- src:16055 | shall be sentenced to imprisonment in a penitentiary.
@ref s 743.1(1) (src:16051-16055)
GIVEN `another provision otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      sentence IS AN Imprisonment
      `the aggregate of two or more terms of less than two years each, to be served one after the other` IS A MAYBE `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.1(1) the person shall be sentenced to imprisonment in a penitentiary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `another provision otherwise provides`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except where otherwise provided" (an "except" gate; the provision that otherwise provides is outside this range) (fork F-13)
        IF sentence EQUALS `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a)
        IF `s 742.1 the sentence of imprisonment is at least that many years` sentence 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b)
        IF `the aggregate is at least two years` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE   -- (c)
        IF `s 742.1 the sentence of imprisonment is at least that many years` sentence 2 EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no term is stated
        IF `the aggregate is at least two years` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the days of the aggregate might carry into a month
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who is sentenced to imprisonment for (a) life, (b) a term of two years or more, or (c) two or more terms of less than two years each ... shall be sentenced to imprisonment in a penitentiary" (the duty's own question: none of the three is met)
    WHERE
        `the aggregate is at least two years` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the aggregate of two or more terms of less than two years each, to be served one after the other`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN JUST agg THEN `s 742.1 the length of time is at least that many years` agg 2

-- src:16057 | (2) Where a person who is sentenced to imprisonment in a penitentiary is, before the expiration of that sentence, sentenced to imprisonment for a term of less than two years, the person shall serve that term in a penitentiary, but if the previous sentence of imprisonment in a penitentiary is set aside, that person shall serve that term in accordance with subsection (3).
@ref s 743.1(2) (src:16057)
GIVEN `the person is sentenced to imprisonment in a penitentiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before the expiration of that sentence the person is sentenced to imprisonment for a term of less than two years` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the previous sentence of imprisonment in a penitentiary is set aside` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.1(2) the person shall serve that term in a penitentiary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the person is sentenced to imprisonment in a penitentiary`)) OR (NOT (`before the expiration of that sentence the person is sentenced to imprisonment for a term of less than two years`))
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person who is sentenced to imprisonment in a penitentiary is, before the expiration of that sentence, sentenced to imprisonment for a term of less than two years" (a duty whose "where" is unmet, fork F-3)
        IF `the previous sentence of imprisonment in a penitentiary is set aside`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but if the previous sentence of imprisonment in a penitentiary is set aside, that person shall serve that term in accordance with subsection (3)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16059 | (3) A person who is sentenced to imprisonment and who is not required to be sentenced as provided in subsection (1) or (2) shall, unless a special prison is prescribed by law, be sentenced to imprisonment in a prison or other place of confinement, other than a penitentiary, within the province in which the person is convicted, in which the sentence of imprisonment may be lawfully executed.
@ref s 743.1(3) (src:16059)
GIVEN `the person is sentenced to imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `required by subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `required by subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `required by subsection (3.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a special prison is prescribed by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.1(3) the person shall be sentenced to imprisonment in a prison or other place of confinement, other than a penitentiary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is sentenced to imprisonment`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who is sentenced to imprisonment" (a duty whose gate is unmet, fork F-3)
        IF `required by subsection (1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `required by subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `required by subsection (3.1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who is not required to be sentenced as provided in subsection (1) or (2)" and "Despite subsection (3)" in subsection (3.1)
        IF `a special prison is prescribed by law`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless a special prison is prescribed by law" (fork F-13)
        IF `required by subsection (1)` EQUALS NOTHING OR `required by subsection (2)` EQUALS NOTHING OR `required by subsection (3.1)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (1), (2) or (3.1) is not decided on these facts
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16059 | (3) A person who is sentenced to imprisonment and who is not required to be sentenced as provided in subsection (1) or (2) shall, unless a special prison is prescribed by law, be sentenced to imprisonment in a prison or other place of confinement, other than a penitentiary, within the province in which the person is convicted, in which the sentence of imprisonment may be lawfully executed.
@ref s 743.1(3) (src:16059)
GIVEN `the province in which the person is convicted` IS A `Province or territory`
      `the province in which the place of confinement is` IS A `Province or territory`
      `the sentence of imprisonment may be lawfully executed in the place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.1(3) the place of confinement is within the province in which the person is convicted, and the sentence may be lawfully executed there` MEANS
    IF `the province in which the person is convicted` EQUALS `the province in which the place of confinement is` AND `the sentence of imprisonment may be lawfully executed in the place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the province in which the person is convicted, in which the sentence of imprisonment may be lawfully executed"

-- src:16061 | (3.1) Despite subsection (3), an offender who is subject to long-term supervision under Part XXIV and is sentenced for another offence during the period of the supervision shall be sentenced to imprisonment in a penitentiary.
@ref s 743.1(3.1) (src:16061)
GIVEN `the offender is subject to long-term supervision under Part XXIV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender is sentenced for another offence during the period of the supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.1(3.1) the offender shall be sentenced to imprisonment in a penitentiary` MEANS
    IF `the offender is subject to long-term supervision under Part XXIV` AND `the offender is sentenced for another offence during the period of the supervision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an offender who is subject to long-term supervision under Part XXIV and is sentenced for another offence during the period of the supervision" (a duty whose relative clause is unmet, fork F-7)

-- src:16063 | (4) Where a person is sentenced to imprisonment in a penitentiary while the person is lawfully imprisoned in a place other than a penitentiary, that person shall, except where otherwise provided, be sent immediately to the penitentiary, and shall serve in the penitentiary the unexpired portion of the term of imprisonment that that person was serving when sentenced to the penitentiary as well as the term of imprisonment for which that person was sentenced to the penitentiary.
@ref s 743.1(4) (src:16063)
GIVEN `the person is sentenced to imprisonment in a penitentiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is lawfully imprisoned in a place other than a penitentiary at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another provision otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.1(4) the person shall be sent immediately to the penitentiary and serve there the unexpired portion of the term being served as well as the new term` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the person is sentenced to imprisonment in a penitentiary`)) OR (NOT (`the person is lawfully imprisoned in a place other than a penitentiary at the time`))
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is sentenced to imprisonment in a penitentiary while the person is lawfully imprisoned in a place other than a penitentiary" (a duty whose "where" is unmet, fork F-3)
        IF `another provision otherwise provides` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except where otherwise provided" (fork F-13)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16065 | (5) Where, at any time, a person who is imprisoned in a prison or place of confinement other than a penitentiary is subject to two or more terms of imprisonment, each of which is for less than two years, that are to be served one after the other, and the aggregate of the unexpired portions of those terms at that time amounts to two years or more, the person shall be transferred to a penitentiary to serve those terms, but if any one or more of such terms is set aside or reduced and the unexpired portions of the remaining term or terms on the day on which that person was transferred under this section amounted to less than two years, that person shall serve that term or terms in accordance with subsection (3).
@ref s 743.1(5) (src:16065)
GIVEN `the person is imprisoned in a prison or place of confinement other than a penitentiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is subject to two or more terms of imprisonment, each for less than two years, to be served one after the other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate of the unexpired portions of those terms at that time` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.1(5) the person shall be transferred to a penitentiary to serve those terms` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the person is imprisoned in a prison or place of confinement other than a penitentiary`)) OR (NOT (`the person is subject to two or more terms of imprisonment, each for less than two years, to be served one after the other`))
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, at any time, a person who is imprisoned in a prison or place of confinement other than a penitentiary is subject to two or more terms of imprisonment, each of which is for less than two years" (a duty whose "where" is unmet, fork F-3)
    ELSE `s 742.1 the length of time is at least that many years` `the aggregate of the unexpired portions of those terms at that time` 2

-- src:16065 | (5) Where, at any time, a person who is imprisoned in a prison or place of confinement other than a penitentiary is subject to two or more terms of imprisonment, each of which is for less than two years, that are to be served one after the other, and the aggregate of the unexpired portions of those terms at that time amounts to two years or more, the person shall be transferred to a penitentiary to serve those terms, but if any one or more of such terms is set aside or reduced and the unexpired portions of the remaining term or terms on the day on which that person was transferred under this section amounted to less than two years, that person shall serve that term or terms in accordance with subsection (3).
@ref s 743.1(5) (src:16065)
GIVEN `a term has been set aside or reduced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate of the unexpired portions of the remaining terms on the day of the transfer` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.1(5) the person shall serve the remaining terms in accordance with subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `a term has been set aside or reduced`
    THEN `the remaining terms are under two years`
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but if any one or more of such terms is set aside or reduced and the unexpired portions of the remaining term or terms ... amounted to less than two years"
    WHERE
        `the remaining terms are under two years` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 742.1 the length of time is at least that many years` `the aggregate of the unexpired portions of the remaining terms on the day of the transfer` 2
            WHEN JUST atLeast THEN JUST (NOT (atLeast))
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the days might carry into a month

DECLARE `s 743.1(6) the day` IS ONE OF
    `s 743.1(6) before the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council`
    `s 743.1(6) on or after the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council`

-- src:16067 | (6) For the purposes of subsection (3), “penitentiary” does not, until a day to be fixed by order of the Governor in Council, include the facility mentioned in subsection 15(2) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act.
@ref s 743.1(6) (src:16067)
GIVEN `the facility is the facility mentioned in subsection 15(2) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A `s 743.1(6) the day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.1(6) the facility is left out of "penitentiary" for the purposes of subsection (3)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the facility is the facility mentioned in subsection 15(2) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the facility mentioned in subsection 15(2) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act"
        IF day EQUALS `s 743.1(6) before the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council` THEN JUST TRUE   -- the "until" bar: the facility is left out until the day
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not, until a day to be fixed by order of the Governor in Council, include the facility" (after the day the bar is gone: the "until" bar of ruling (d) of 2026-11-05; whether the facility is then included is not said)

§ `Sections 743.2 to 743.5 -- Reports, non-communication, regulations of the institution, youth sentences`

-- src:16069 | 743.2 A court that sentences or commits a person to penitentiary shall forward to the Correctional Service of Canada its reasons and recommendation relating to the sentence or committal, any relevant reports that were submitted to the court, and any other information relevant to administering the sentence or committal.
@ref s 743.2 (src:16069)
GIVEN `the court sentences or commits a person to penitentiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it forwards to the Correctional Service of Canada its reasons and recommendation relating to the sentence or committal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it forwards any relevant reports that were submitted to the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it forwards any other information relevant to administering the sentence or committal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.2 the court has forwarded to the Correctional Service of Canada what the section requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the court sentences or commits a person to penitentiary`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A court that sentences or commits a person to penitentiary" (a duty whose relative clause is unmet, fork F-7)
        IF `it forwards to the Correctional Service of Canada its reasons and recommendation relating to the sentence or committal` AND `it forwards any relevant reports that were submitted to the court` AND `it forwards any other information relevant to administering the sentence or committal`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall forward ... its reasons and recommendation ..., any relevant reports ..., and any other information" (a list joined by "and")

DECLARE `s 743.2 act` IS ONE OF `s 743.2 forward the reasons, recommendation, reports and information`

-- src:16069 | 743.2 A court that sentences or commits a person to penitentiary shall forward to the Correctional Service of Canada its reasons and recommendation relating to the sentence or committal, any relevant reports that were submitted to the court, and any other information relevant to administering the sentence or committal.
@ref s 743.2 (src:16069)
`s 743.2 the court shall forward the reasons, recommendation, reports and information` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 743.2 forward the reasons, recommendation, reports and information`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the court did not forward its reasons and recommendation, the relevant reports and the other relevant information to the Correctional Service of Canada"

-- src:16071 | 743.21 (1) The sentencing judge may issue an order prohibiting the offender from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order during the custodial period of the sentence, except in accordance with any conditions specified in the order that the sentencing judge considers necessary.
@ref s 743.21(1) (src:16071)
GIVEN `the person who issues the order is the sentencing judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is made for the custodial period of the sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.21(1) the sentencing judge may issue an order prohibiting the offender from communicating with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order` MEANS
    IF `the person who issues the order is the sentencing judge` AND `the order is made for the custodial period of the sentence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The sentencing judge may issue an order ... during the custodial period of the sentence"

-- src:16071 | 743.21 (1) The sentencing judge may issue an order prohibiting the offender from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order during the custodial period of the sentence, except in accordance with any conditions specified in the order that the sentencing judge considers necessary.
@ref s 743.21(1) (src:16071)
GIVEN `an order has been issued under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is a victim, a witness or another person identified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time is during the custodial period of the sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the communication is in accordance with the conditions specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.21(1) the offender is barred from communicating with the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an order has been issued under subsection (1)`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar arises "prohibiting the offender" only under an order (a bar whose gate is unmet)
        IF NOT (`the other person is a victim, a witness or another person identified in the order`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any victim, witness or other person identified in the order"
        IF NOT (`the time is during the custodial period of the sentence`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "during the custodial period of the sentence" (a period in the text's own words, ruling (a))
        IF `the communication is in accordance with the conditions specified in the order` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in accordance with any conditions specified in the order that the sentencing judge considers necessary" (fork F-13)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16073 | (2) Every person who fails, without lawful excuse, to comply with the order
-- src:16074 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years; or
-- src:16075 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 743.21(2) (src:16073-16075)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.21(2) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to comply with the order` AND (NOT (`the person has a lawful excuse`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who fails, without lawful excuse, to comply with the order" (an offence-creating sentence whose elements are unmet, fork F-7)

-- The punishment limbs. The text states "a term not exceeding two years" for the indictable limb and, for the summary limb, only the mode:
-- section 787 (outside this range) gives the general maximum.
-- src:16074 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years; or
-- src:16075 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 743.21(2) (src:16074-16075)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 743.21(2) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- src:16077 | 743.3 A sentence of imprisonment shall be served in accordance with the enactments and rules that govern the institution to which the prisoner is sentenced.
@ref s 743.3 (src:16077)
GIVEN `the sentence is a sentence of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enactments and rules applied are those that govern the institution to which the prisoner is sentenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.3 the sentence is served as the section requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the sentence is a sentence of imprisonment`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A sentence of imprisonment"
        IF `the enactments and rules applied are those that govern the institution to which the prisoner is sentenced` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be served in accordance with the enactments and rules that govern the institution to which the prisoner is sentenced" (fork F-14)

-- src:16080 | 743.5 (1) If a young person or an adult is or has been sentenced to a term of imprisonment for an offence while subject to a disposition made under paragraph 20(1)(k) or (k.1) of the Young Offenders Act, chapter Y-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1985, or a youth sentence imposed under paragraph 42(2)(n), (o), (q) or (r) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act, the remaining portion of the disposition or youth sentence shall be dealt with, for all purposes under this Act or any other Act of Parliament, as if it had been a sentence imposed under this Act.
@ref s 743.5(1) (src:16080)
GIVEN `a young person or an adult is or has been sentenced to a term of imprisonment for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sentence was imposed while the person was subject to a disposition under paragraph 20(1)(k) or (k.1) of the Young Offenders Act, or a youth sentence under paragraph 42(2)(n), (o), (q) or (r) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.5(1) the remaining portion of the disposition or youth sentence is dealt with as if it had been a sentence imposed under this Act` MEANS
    IF `a young person or an adult is or has been sentenced to a term of imprisonment for an offence` AND `the sentence was imposed while the person was subject to a disposition under paragraph 20(1)(k) or (k.1) of the Young Offenders Act, or a youth sentence under paragraph 42(2)(n), (o), (q) or (r) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a young person or an adult is or has been sentenced to a term of imprisonment for an offence while subject to a disposition ... or a youth sentence" (the provision's own question, "if" unmet)

-- src:16082 | (2) If a disposition is made under paragraph 20(1)(k) or (k.1) of the Young Offenders Act, chapter Y-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1985, with respect to a person or a youth sentence is imposed on a person under paragraph 42(2)(n), (o), (q) or (r) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act while the young person or adult is under sentence of imprisonment imposed under an Act of Parliament other than the Youth Criminal Justice Act, the disposition or youth sentence shall be dealt with, for all purposes under this Act or any other Act of Parliament, as if it had been a sentence imposed under this Act.
@ref s 743.5(2) (src:16082)
GIVEN `a disposition under paragraph 20(1)(k) or (k.1) of the Young Offenders Act is made, or a youth sentence under paragraph 42(2)(n), (o), (q) or (r) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the person is under sentence of imprisonment imposed under an Act of Parliament other than the Youth Criminal Justice Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.5(2) the disposition or youth sentence is dealt with as if it had been a sentence imposed under this Act` MEANS
    IF `a disposition under paragraph 20(1)(k) or (k.1) of the Young Offenders Act is made, or a youth sentence under paragraph 42(2)(n), (o), (q) or (r) of the Youth Criminal Justice Act is imposed` AND `at the time the person is under sentence of imprisonment imposed under an Act of Parliament other than the Youth Criminal Justice Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a disposition is made ... or a youth sentence is imposed ... while the young person or adult is under sentence of imprisonment imposed under an Act of Parliament other than the Youth Criminal Justice Act" (the provision's own question, "if" unmet)

DECLARE `s 743.5(3) combination` IS ONE OF
    `s 743.5(3)(a) the remainder of the youth sentence or disposition and the subsequent term of imprisonment, for the purposes of subsection (1)`
    `s 743.5(3)(b) the term of imprisonment and the subsequent youth sentence or disposition, for the purposes of subsection (2)`
    `s 743.5(3) any other combination`

-- src:16084 | (3) For greater certainty, the following are deemed to constitute one sentence of imprisonment for the purposes of section 139 of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act:
-- src:16085 | (a) for the purposes of subsection (1), the remainder of the youth sentence or disposition and the subsequent term of imprisonment; and
-- src:16086 | (b) for the purposes of subsection (2), the term of imprisonment and the subsequent youth sentence or disposition.
@ref s 743.5(3) (src:16084-16086)
GIVEN combination IS A `s 743.5(3) combination`
      `the purpose is that of section 139 of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.5(3) the combination is deemed to constitute one sentence of imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is that of section 139 of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` AND NOT (combination EQUALS `s 743.5(3) any other combination`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the following are deemed to constitute one sentence of imprisonment for the purposes of section 139 of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act"

§ `Section 743.6 -- Power of court to delay parole`

-- The sentence tests shared by subsections (1) to (1.2): "a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more, including a sentence of imprisonment for life imposed otherwise than as a minimum punishment"
-- (subsection (1.2) drops the words "imposed otherwise than as a minimum punishment"; the second input is then not read).
GIVEN sentence IS AN Imprisonment
      `the life sentence was imposed as a minimum punishment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.6 the sentence is of two years or more, including life imposed otherwise than as a minimum punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER sentence
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no term is stated
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST (NOT (`the life sentence was imposed as a minimum punishment`))
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN `s 742.1 the length of time is at least that many years` term 2

-- src:16090 | 743.6 (1) Notwithstanding subsection 120(1) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act, where an offender receives, on or after November 1, 1992, a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more, including a sentence of imprisonment for life imposed otherwise than as a minimum punishment, on conviction for an offence set out in Schedule I or II to that Act that was prosecuted by way of indictment, the court may, if satisfied, having regard to the circumstances of the commission of the offence and the character and circumstances of the offender, that the expression of society’s denunciation of the offence or the objective of specific or general deterrence so requires, order that the portion of the sentence that must be served before the offender may be released on full parole is one half of the sentence or ten years, whichever is less.
@ref s 743.6(1) (src:16090)
GIVEN `the date of the sentence` IS A DATE
      sentence IS AN Imprisonment
      `the life sentence was imposed as a minimum punishment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is set out in Schedule I or II to the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mode in which the offence was prosecuted` IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `the court is satisfied, having regard to the circumstances of the commission of the offence and the character and circumstances of the offender, that the expression of society's denunciation of the offence or the objective of specific or general deterrence so requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.6(1) the court may order that the portion of the sentence that must be served before the offender may be released on full parole is one half of the sentence or ten years, whichever is less` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date of the sentence` LESS THAN (Date 1 11 1992)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an offender receives, on or after November 1, 1992, a sentence" (a "where" gate on a "may", ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF `s 743.6 the sentence is of two years or more, including life imposed otherwise than as a minimum punishment` sentence `the life sentence was imposed as a minimum punishment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an offender receives ... a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more, including a sentence of imprisonment for life imposed otherwise than as a minimum punishment" (a "where" gate on a "may", ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF (NOT (`the offence is set out in Schedule I or II to the Corrections and Conditional Release Act`)) OR (NOT (`the mode in which the offence was prosecuted` EQUALS `by indictment`))
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on conviction for an offence set out in Schedule I or II to that Act that was prosecuted by way of indictment" (a "where" gate on a "may", ruling (b); listed, group (i)) (fork F-16)
        IF `s 743.6 the sentence is of two years or more, including life imposed otherwise than as a minimum punishment` sentence `the life sentence was imposed as a minimum punishment` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the term is not stated, or its days might carry into a month
        IF `the court is satisfied, having regard to the circumstances of the commission of the offence and the character and circumstances of the offender, that the expression of society's denunciation of the offence or the objective of specific or general deterrence so requires`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may, if satisfied ... that the expression of society's denunciation of the offence or the objective of specific or general deterrence so requires" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:16092 | (1.1) Notwithstanding section 120 of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act, where an offender receives a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more, including a sentence of imprisonment for life imposed otherwise than as a minimum punishment, on conviction for a criminal organization offence other than an offence under section 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13, the court may order that the portion of the sentence that must be served before the offender may be released on full parole is one half of the sentence or ten years, whichever is less.
@ref s 743.6(1.1) (src:16092)
GIVEN sentence IS AN Imprisonment
      `the life sentence was imposed as a minimum punishment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 criminal organization offence: the offence is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.6(1.1) the court may order that the portion of the sentence that must be served before the offender may be released on full parole is one half of the sentence or ten years, whichever is less` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 743.6 the sentence is of two years or more, including life imposed otherwise than as a minimum punishment` sentence `the life sentence was imposed as a minimum punishment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an offender receives a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more, including a sentence of imprisonment for life imposed otherwise than as a minimum punishment" (a "where" gate on a "may", ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF elem (offence's `section`) (LIST 467.11, 467.111, 467.12, 467.13)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a criminal organization offence other than an offence under section 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13" (a "where" gate on a "may", ruling (b); listed, group (i)) (fork F-15)
        IF `s 2 criminal organization offence: the offence is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on conviction for a criminal organization offence" (a "where" gate on a "may", ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF `s 743.6 the sentence is of two years or more, including life imposed otherwise than as a minimum punishment` sentence `the life sentence was imposed as a minimum punishment` EQUALS NOTHING OR `s 2 criminal organization offence: the offence is one` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the term is not stated, or section 2's "criminal organization offence" is not covered on these facts
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16094 | (1.2) Notwithstanding section 120 of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act, where an offender receives a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more, including a sentence of imprisonment for life, on conviction for a terrorism offence or an offence under section 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13, the court shall order that the portion of the sentence that must be served before the offender may be released on full parole is one half of the sentence or ten years, whichever is less, unless the court is satisfied, having regard to the circumstances of the commission of the offence and the character and circumstances of the offender, that the expression of society’s denunciation of the offence and the objectives of specific and general deterrence would be adequately served by a period of parole ineligibility determined in accordance with the Corrections and Conditional Release Act.
@ref s 743.6(1.2) (src:16094)
GIVEN sentence IS AN Imprisonment
      `s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the court is satisfied, having regard to the circumstances of the commission of the offence and the character and circumstances of the offender, that the expression of society's denunciation of the offence and the objectives of specific and general deterrence would be adequately served by a period of parole ineligibility determined in accordance with the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.6(1.2) the court shall order that the portion of the sentence that must be served before the offender may be released on full parole is one half of the sentence or ten years, whichever is less` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 743.6 the sentence is of two years or more, including life imposed otherwise than as a minimum punishment` sentence FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an offender receives a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more, including a sentence of imprisonment for life" (a "where" gate on a duty, ruling (b))
        IF (NOT (elem (offence's `section`) (LIST 467.11, 467.111, 467.12, 467.13))) AND (`s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on conviction for a terrorism offence or an offence under section 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13" (a "where" gate on a duty, ruling (b))
        IF `the court is satisfied, having regard to the circumstances of the commission of the offence and the character and circumstances of the offender, that the expression of society's denunciation of the offence and the objectives of specific and general deterrence would be adequately served by a period of parole ineligibility determined in accordance with the Corrections and Conditional Release Act`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the court is satisfied ... that the expression of society's denunciation of the offence and the objectives of specific and general deterrence would be adequately served by a period of parole ineligibility determined in accordance with the Corrections and Conditional Release Act" (fork F-13)
        IF (`s 743.6 the sentence is of two years or more, including life imposed otherwise than as a minimum punishment` sentence FALSE EQUALS NOTHING) OR ((`s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is one` EQUALS NOTHING) AND (NOT (elem (offence's `section`) (LIST 467.11, 467.111, 467.12, 467.13))))
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the term is not stated, or section 2's "terrorism offence" is not covered on these facts
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 743.6(2) principle` IS ONE OF
    `s 743.6(2) denunciation`
    `s 743.6(2) specific deterrence`
    `s 743.6(2) general deterrence`
    `s 743.6(2) rehabilitation of the offender`
    `s 743.6(2) another principle`

-- src:16096 | (2) For greater certainty, the paramount principles which are to guide the court under this section are denunciation and specific or general deterrence, with rehabilitation of the offender, in all cases, being subordinate to these paramount principles.
@ref s 743.6(2) (src:16096)
GIVEN principle IS A `s 743.6(2) principle`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.6(2) the principle is one of the paramount principles that guide the court under section 743.6` MEANS
    CONSIDER principle
    WHEN `s 743.6(2) denunciation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 743.6(2) specific deterrence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 743.6(2) general deterrence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 743.6(2) rehabilitation of the offender` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with rehabilitation of the offender, in all cases, being subordinate to these paramount principles"
    WHEN `s 743.6(2) another principle` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names the paramount principles and the one it ranks below them

-- The portion an order under (1), (1.1) or (1.2) sets: "one half of the sentence or ten years, whichever is less", in months.
-- A term with days is not converted: the text does not say how many days make a month.
-- src:16090 | 743.6 (1) Notwithstanding subsection 120(1) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act, where an offender receives, on or after November 1, 1992, a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more, including a sentence of imprisonment for life imposed otherwise than as a minimum punishment, on conviction for an offence set out in Schedule I or II to that Act that was prosecuted by way of indictment, the court may, if satisfied, having regard to the circumstances of the commission of the offence and the character and circumstances of the offender, that the expression of society’s denunciation of the offence or the objective of specific or general deterrence so requires, order that the portion of the sentence that must be served before the offender may be released on full parole is one half of the sentence or ten years, whichever is less.
@ref s 743.6(1) (src:16090)
GIVEN sentence IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 743.6 the months of the sentence that must be served before the offender may be released on full parole under the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER sentence
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no term is stated
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST 120   -- ten years: a life sentence has no half
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN
        IF term's days EQUALS 0 AND NOT (term's `less a day`)
        THEN JUST (min ((term's years TIMES 12 PLUS term's months) DIVIDED BY 2) 120)
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): days are not converted to months

-- The seam for section 675 and 676 (part ccc24): was a delay in eligibility for parole ordered under section 743.6? The three inputs say whether an order
-- was made under subsection (1), (1.1) and (1.2). JUST FALSE only when all three inputs are JUST FALSE: an order under any one of them makes the answer JUST TRUE,
-- and a missing input leaves the answer NOTHING (an order may have been made under the subsection that is not known).
GIVEN `an order was made under subsection 743.6(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an order was made under subsection 743.6(1.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an order was made under subsection 743.6(1.2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.6 the court ordered a delay in eligibility for parole` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an order was made under subsection 743.6(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `an order was made under subsection 743.6(1.1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `an order was made under subsection 743.6(1.2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `an order was made under subsection 743.6(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `an order was made under subsection 743.6(1.1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `an order was made under subsection 743.6(1.2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the only orders section 743.6 provides for are those under subsections (1), (1.1) and (1.2); the three inputs say none was made
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): at least one of the three orders is not known

§ `Section 744 -- Delivery of offender to keeper of prison`

DECLARE `s 744 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 744 arrest the person named or described in the warrant`
    `s 744 convey the person to the prison mentioned in the warrant and deliver the person, with the warrant, to the keeper of the prison`
    `s 744 give a receipt in Form 43`

-- src:16100 | 744 A peace officer or other person to whom a warrant of committal authorized by this or any other Act of Parliament is directed shall arrest the person named or described therein, if it is necessary to do so in order to take that person into custody, convey that person to the prison mentioned in the warrant and deliver that person, together with the warrant, to the keeper of the prison who shall thereupon give to the peace officer or other person who delivers the prisoner a receipt in Form 43 setting out the state and condition of the prisoner when delivered into custody.
@ref s 744 (src:16100)
GIVEN `the person to whom a warrant of committal authorized by this or any other Act of Parliament is directed is a peace officer or other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is necessary to arrest the person in order to take the person into custody` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 744 the peace officer or other person shall arrest the person named or described in the warrant` MEANS
    IF `the person to whom a warrant of committal authorized by this or any other Act of Parliament is directed is a peace officer or other person` AND `it is necessary to arrest the person in order to take the person into custody`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall arrest the person named or described therein, if it is necessary to do so in order to take that person into custody" (a duty whose "if" is unmet, fork F-3)

-- src:16100 | 744 A peace officer or other person to whom a warrant of committal authorized by this or any other Act of Parliament is directed shall arrest the person named or described therein, if it is necessary to do so in order to take that person into custody, convey that person to the prison mentioned in the warrant and deliver that person, together with the warrant, to the keeper of the prison who shall thereupon give to the peace officer or other person who delivers the prisoner a receipt in Form 43 setting out the state and condition of the prisoner when delivered into custody.
@ref s 744 (src:16100)
GIVEN `the person to whom a warrant of committal authorized by this or any other Act of Parliament is directed is a peace officer or other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 744 the peace officer or other person shall convey the person to the prison mentioned in the warrant and deliver the person, together with the warrant, to the keeper of the prison` MEANS
    IF `the person to whom a warrant of committal authorized by this or any other Act of Parliament is directed is a peace officer or other person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A peace officer or other person to whom a warrant of committal ... is directed shall" (a duty whose relative clause is unmet, fork F-7)

-- src:16100 | 744 A peace officer or other person to whom a warrant of committal authorized by this or any other Act of Parliament is directed shall arrest the person named or described therein, if it is necessary to do so in order to take that person into custody, convey that person to the prison mentioned in the warrant and deliver that person, together with the warrant, to the keeper of the prison who shall thereupon give to the peace officer or other person who delivers the prisoner a receipt in Form 43 setting out the state and condition of the prisoner when delivered into custody.
@ref s 744 (src:16100)
GIVEN `the keeper of the prison gives the peace officer or other person a receipt in Form 43 setting out the state and condition of the prisoner when delivered into custody` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 744 the keeper of the prison shall give a receipt in Form 43` MEANS
    IF `the keeper of the prison gives the peace officer or other person a receipt in Form 43 setting out the state and condition of the prisoner when delivered into custody`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the keeper of the prison who shall thereupon give to the peace officer or other person who delivers the prisoner a receipt in Form 43 setting out the state and condition of the prisoner when delivered into custody" (a duty not done)

-- The same duties as one regulative rule (the peace officer delivers, then the keeper gives a receipt in Form 43; no time limit is stated).
-- src:16100 | 744 A peace officer or other person to whom a warrant of committal authorized by this or any other Act of Parliament is directed shall arrest the person named or described therein, if it is necessary to do so in order to take that person into custody, convey that person to the prison mentioned in the warrant and deliver that person, together with the warrant, to the keeper of the prison who shall thereupon give to the peace officer or other person who delivers the prisoner a receipt in Form 43 setting out the state and condition of the prisoner when delivered into custody.
@ref s 744 (src:16100)
`s 744 the peace officer or other person shall deliver the person to the keeper of the prison, and the keeper shall give a receipt` MEANS
    PARTY `a peace officer`
    MUST `s 744 convey the person to the prison mentioned in the warrant and deliver the person, with the warrant, to the keeper of the prison`
    HENCE PARTY `the keeper of a prison`
          MUST `s 744 give a receipt in Form 43`
          HENCE FULFILLED
          LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the keeper of the prison did not give a receipt in Form 43"
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the person was not delivered to the keeper of the prison with the warrant"
